==============================================================================
[B] D1 (Zegarlinski C(beta)<1): exact window, disjoint from beta=2.5
==============================================================================
  delta_kj >= 2*beta per straddling plaquette (that IS the plaquette weight 2*beta*[0,1])
  C(beta) >= 2*beta*deg_future ;  deg_future = 3 in 4D (faces +mu, mu=1..4, ordered)
  window of D1:  2*beta*deg < 1  <=>  beta < 1/(2*deg)
    deg=1:  C(beta)>= 2*beta ;  D1 window beta < 0.500000   ;  2.5/bmax =   5.000x
    deg=3:  C(beta)>= 6*beta ;  D1 window beta < 0.166667   ;  2.5/bmax =  15.000x
    deg=4:  C(beta)>= 8*beta ;  D1 window beta < 0.125000   ;  2.5/bmax =  20.000x
  at beta=2.5:
    deg=3:  C >=   15.000   (corpus quotes C~15)   => C<1 FALSE
    deg=4:  C >=   20.000   (corpus quotes C~15)   => C<1 FALSE
  => D1 fails for beta > 1/6 ;  beta=2.5 is 15x outside.  D1 is a ROUTE, not the statement.

