==============================================================================
[I] full LSI =/=> D3 : the E|grad_par F|^2 leakage (exact toy)
==============================================================================
  mu = N(0,s^2) on the coarse coord a  x  N(0,1) on the fiber coord b   (Gaussian => full LSI, lam=1)
  F = a + b  (general, NOT xi-only).  Exact:  Var= s^2+1 ; E|grad_par F|^2 = s^2 ; E|grad_perp F|^2 = 1
   s     Var(F)     (1/1)(E|gp|^2+E|gq|^2)   (1/1)E|gq|^2      Var <= E|gq|^2 ?
     0.1      1.0100                 1.0100           1.0000      NO
     1.0      2.0000                 2.0000           1.0000      NO
    10.0    101.0000               101.0000           1.0000      NO
   100.0  10001.0000             10001.0000           1.0000      NO
  1000.0  1000001.0000           1000001.0000           1.0000      NO
  => the full LSI bounds Var by (E|gp|^2+E|gq|^2); it does NOT bound it by E|gq|^2 alone.
     The obstruction is exactly the leakage the corpus calls 'no grad_perp bound gives a
     grad_par bound' (PROOF-IR-H1 Sec.1) -- here run in reverse.  So D3 is NOT a corollary
     of SZZ; and for xi-only f it IS (Var_mu(f) <= lam^-1 E|grad_perp f|^2), which is the
     RESTRICTED form the assembly cannot use.

